IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2: s 154 (disqualification on conviction of certain offences),
-- s 155 (persistent default in delivering documents to the Registrar), s 155A (director of 3 or more companies struck off in 5 years).
-- s 153 is shown repealed (a coverage row only).
--
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say. A bar is named as a bar: JUST TRUE means "barred".

§ `Section 154: disqualification on conviction of certain offences`

DECLARE `s 154(5) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): a person is subject to the disqualifications in (3) if (a)(i) convicted of an offence involving fraud or dishonesty punishable with
-- imprisonment for 3 months or more; (ii) of an offence under Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001, convicted on or after 1 July 2015;
-- (iii) of an offence under s 50, 51, 53, 54, 55 or 55A of the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act 1992,
-- convicted on or after the commencement of s 56 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025; or (b) subject to a civil penalty
-- under s 232 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 on or after 1 July 2015.
-- src:12393 | 154.—(1) A person is subject to the disqualifications provided in
-- src:12394 | subsection (3) if —
-- src:12396 | (a) the person is convicted of any of the following offences:
-- src:12398 | (i) any offence, whether in Singapore or elsewhere,
-- src:12399 | involving fraud or dishonesty punishable with
-- src:12400 | imprisonment for 3 months or more;
-- src:12402 | (ii) any offence under Part 12 of the Securities and
-- src:12403 | Futures Act 2001, where the conviction was on or
-- src:12404 | after 1 July 2015;
-- src:12411 | (iii) an offence under section 50, 51, 53, 54, 55 or 55A of
-- src:12412 | the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious
-- src:12413 | Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act 1992, where
-- src:12414 | the conviction is on or after the date of
-- src:12415 | commencement of section 56 of the Corporate and
-- src:12416 | Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025; or
-- src:12420 | (b) the person is subject to the imposition of a civil penalty
-- src:12421 | under section 232 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001
-- src:12422 | on or after 1 July 2015.
@ref s 154(1) (src:12393-12422)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, involving fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is convicted of an offence under Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of an offence under section 50, 51, 53, 54, 55 or 55A of the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the conviction` IS A DATE
      `the date of commencement of section 56 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025` IS A DATE
      `the person is subject to the imposition of a civil penalty under section 232 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the civil penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(1) the person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is convicted of an offence, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, involving fraud or dishonesty` AND `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` AT LEAST 3)
       OR (`the person is convicted of an offence under Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` AND `the date of the conviction` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2015)
       OR (`the person is convicted of an offence under section 50, 51, 53, 54, 55 or 55A of the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act 1992` AND `the date of the conviction` AT LEAST `the date of commencement of section 56 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025`)
       OR (`the person is subject to the imposition of a civil penalty under section 232 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001` AND `the date the civil penalty is imposed` AT LEAST Date 1 7 2015)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is subject to the disqualifications provided in subsection (3) if -- (a) the person is convicted of any of the following offences ...; or (b) the person is subject to the imposition of a civil penalty" -- a condition introduced with "if" that fails (marginal reading (a)); subsection (2) is a separate route

-- (2): the court may, in addition to any other sentence, make a disqualification order against a person convicted in Singapore of one of three kinds of offence.
DECLARE `s 154(2) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 154(2)(a) an offence in connection with the formation or management of a corporation`
    `s 154(2)(b) an offence under section 157 or 396B`
    `s 154(2)(c) an offence under section 237 or 239 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 154(2) some other offence`

-- src:12426 | (2) The court may, in addition to any other sentence imposed, make
-- src:12427 | a disqualification order against any person who is convicted in
-- src:12428 | Singapore of any of the following offences:
-- src:12430 | (a) any offence in connection with the formation or
-- src:12431 | management of a corporation;
-- src:12433 | (b) any offence under section 157 or 396B;
-- src:12435 | (c) any offence under section 237 or 239 of the Insolvency,
-- src:12436 | Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 154(2) (src:12426-12436)
GIVEN `the person is convicted in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence` IS A `s 154(2) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(2) the court may make a disqualification order against the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted in Singapore` AND (NOT (`the offence` EQUALS `s 154(2) some other offence`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may, in addition to any other sentence imposed, make a disqualification order against any person who is convicted in Singapore of any of the following offences" -- a grant ("may") limited to the listed offences and to a conviction in Singapore (grant ruling of 2026-11-12; list not closed with "only")

-- src:12518 | (8) Without affecting section 409, a District Court may make a
-- src:12519 | disqualification order under this section.
@ref s 154(8) (src:12518-12519)
GIVEN `the court is a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(8) a District Court may make a disqualification order under the section` MEANS
    IF `the court is a District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a District Court may make a disqualification order under this section" names one court and says nothing of the others (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (4): when the disqualifications take effect and how long they last.
DECLARE `s 154(4) case` IS ONE OF
    `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment`
    `s 154(4)(b) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) and sentenced to imprisonment`
    `s 154(4)(c) subject to the imposition of a civil penalty on or after 1 July 2015`

-- src:12457 | (4) The disqualifications in subsection (3) —
-- src:12459 | (a) in a case where the disqualified person has been convicted
-- src:12460 | of any offence mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) but has
-- src:12461 | not been sentenced to imprisonment — take effect upon
-- src:12466 | conviction and continue for a period of 5 years or for such
-- src:12467 | shorter period as the court may order under subsection (2);
-- src:12469 | (b) in a case where the disqualified person has been convicted
-- src:12470 | of any offence mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) and has
-- src:12471 | been sentenced to imprisonment — take effect upon
-- src:12472 | conviction and continue for a period of 5 years after his
-- src:12473 | or her release from prison; or
-- src:12475 | (c) in a case where the disqualified person is subject, on or
-- src:12476 | after 1 July 2015, to the imposition of a civil penalty under
-- src:12477 | section 232 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 — take
-- src:12478 | effect upon the imposition of the civil penalty and continue
-- src:12479 | for a period of 5 years after the imposition of the civil
-- src:12480 | penalty.
@ref s 154(4) (src:12457-12480)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `s 154(4) case`
      `the date of the conviction` IS A DATE
      `the date the person is released from prison` IS A DATE
      `the date the civil penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 154(4) the date the disqualification takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`
    WHEN `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment` THEN `the date of the conviction`
    WHEN `s 154(4)(b) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) and sentenced to imprisonment` THEN `the date of the conviction`
    WHEN `s 154(4)(c) subject to the imposition of a civil penalty on or after 1 July 2015` THEN `the date the civil penalty is imposed`

@ref s 154(4) (src:12457-12480)
GIVEN `the case` IS A `s 154(4) case`
      `the date of the conviction` IS A DATE
      `the date the person is released from prison` IS A DATE
      `the date the civil penalty is imposed` IS A DATE
      `the court ordered a shorter period under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period the court ordered, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 154(4) the last day of the disqualification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`
    WHEN `s 154(4)(a) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) but not sentenced to imprisonment` THEN
        IF `the court ordered a shorter period under subsection (2)`
        THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the conviction` `the shorter period the court ordered, in months` Months
        ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the conviction` 5 Years
    WHEN `s 154(4)(b) convicted of an offence in subsection (1) or (2) and sentenced to imprisonment` THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the person is released from prison` 5 Years
    WHEN `s 154(4)(c) subject to the imposition of a civil penalty on or after 1 July 2015` THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the civil penalty is imposed` 5 Years

@ref s 154(4) (src:12457-12480)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the disqualification takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the disqualification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(4) the date asked is within the period of the disqualification` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date the disqualification takes effect` AND `the date asked` AT MOST `the last day of the disqualification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "take effect upon conviction and continue for a period of 5 years or for such shorter period as the court may order" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (3): subject to permission, a person disqualified under (1) or by an order under (2) must not act as a director or take part in the management.
-- src:12440 | (3) Subject to any permission which the Court may give pursuant to
-- src:12441 | an application under subsection (6), a person who —
-- src:12443 | (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or
-- src:12445 | (b) has had a disqualification order made against him or her
-- src:12446 | under subsection (2),
-- src:12448 | must not act as a director, or take part (whether directly or indirectly)
-- src:12449 | in the management of a company, or of a foreign company to which
-- src:12450 | Division 2 of Part 11 applies, during the period of the disqualification
-- src:12451 | or disqualification order.
@ref s 154(3) (src:12440-12451)
GIVEN `the person is disqualified under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has had a disqualification order made against him or her under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked is within the period of the disqualification or disqualification order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(3) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is disqualified under subsection (1)` OR `the person has had a disqualification order made against him or her under subsection (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or (b) has had a disqualification order made against him or her under subsection (2)" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `the Court has given the person permission under subsection (6)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to any permission which the Court may give pursuant to an application under subsection (6)" -- the permission was given
          ELSE (IF NOT `the date asked is within the period of the disqualification or disqualification order`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the period of the disqualification or disqualification order" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
                ELSE (IF `the body is a company, or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies`
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company, or ... a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies" names the bodies and says nothing of others

-- (5): the offence of contravening (3).
-- src:12484 | (5) A person who contravenes subsection (3) shall be guilty of an
-- src:12485 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:12486 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:12487 | both.
@ref s 154(5) (src:12484-12487)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "A person who contravenes subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 154(5) (src:12484-12487)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 154(5) penalty`
`s 154(5) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 154(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 154(5) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (6): a disqualified person may apply to the Court for permission, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice.
-- src:12491 | (6) A person who —
-- src:12493 | (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or
-- src:12495 | (b) has had a disqualification order made against him or her
-- src:12496 | under subsection (2),
-- src:12498 | may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director, or to take
-- src:12499 | part (whether directly or indirectly) in the management of a company,
-- src:12500 | or of a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies, during
-- src:12501 | the period of the disqualification or disqualification order, upon
-- src:12502 | giving the Minister not less than 14 days’ notice of his or her intention
-- src:12503 | to apply for such permission.
@ref s 154(6) (src:12491-12503)
GIVEN `the person is disqualified under subsection (1) or has had a disqualification order made against him or her under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(6) the person may apply to the Court for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` MEANS
    IF `the person is disqualified under subsection (1) or has had a disqualification order made against him or her under subsection (2)`
    THEN (IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court` 14 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to the Court for permission ..., upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice of his or her intention to apply" -- an "upon" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05 counts it as "where") that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or (b) has had a disqualification order made" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- src:12509 | (7) On the hearing of any application under subsection (6), the
-- src:12510 | Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the
-- src:12511 | granting of the application.
@ref s 154(7) (src:12509-12511)
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 154(7) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is of an application under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of any application under subsection (6), the Minister may be represented" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

DECLARE `s 154(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 154(3) act as a director, or take part in the management of a company, during the period of the disqualification`

-- src:12440 | (3) Subject to any permission which the Court may give pursuant to
-- src:12441 | an application under subsection (6), a person who —
-- src:12443 | (a) is disqualified under subsection (1); or
-- src:12445 | (b) has had a disqualification order made against him or her
-- src:12446 | under subsection (2),
-- src:12448 | must not act as a director, or take part (whether directly or indirectly)
-- src:12449 | in the management of a company, or of a foreign company to which
-- src:12450 | Division 2 of Part 11 applies, during the period of the disqualification
-- src:12451 | or disqualification order.
@ref s 154(3) (src:12440-12451)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 154(3) act`
`s 154(3) a disqualified person must not act as a director or take part in the management of a company` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 154(3) act as a director, or take part in the management of a company, during the period of the disqualification`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person disqualified under section 154 acted as a director or took part in the management of a company during the period of the disqualification"

§ `Section 155: persistent default in relation to delivery of documents to the Registrar`

DECLARE `s 155(1) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (2): any provision requiring a return, account or other document to be filed with, delivered or sent to the Registrar, or notice to be given to the Registrar.
-- src:12545 | (2) Any provision of this Act which requires any return, account or
-- src:12546 | other document to be filed with, delivered or sent, or notice of any
-- src:12547 | matter to be given, to the Registrar is a relevant requirement of this
-- src:12548 | Act for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 155(2) (src:12545-12548)
GIVEN `the provision requires a return, account or other document to be filed with, delivered or sent to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision requires notice of any matter to be given to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(2) the provision is a relevant requirement of this Act for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF `the provision requires a return, account or other document to be filed with, delivered or sent to the Registrar` OR `the provision requires notice of any matter to be given to the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision of this Act which requires any return, account or other document to be filed ... is a relevant requirement" says nothing of other provisions

-- (5) a conviction under s 154(2)(a) is not treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement; (8) no account of an offence committed or begun before 15 May 1984.
-- src:12569 | (5) For the purpose of this section, a conviction for an offence under
-- src:12570 | section 154(2)(a) is not to be treated as an offence in relation to a
-- src:12571 | relevant requirement of this Act.
@ref s 155(5) (src:12569-12571)
GIVEN `the conviction is for an offence under section 154(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(5) the conviction is treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the conviction is for an offence under section 154(2)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a conviction for an offence under section 154(2)(a) is not to be treated as an offence in relation to a relevant requirement of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes one kind of conviction and says nothing of the others

-- src:12589 | (8) No account is to be taken for the purposes of this section of any
-- src:12590 | offence which was committed or, in the case of a continuing offence,
-- src:12591 | began before 15 May 1984.
@ref s 155(8) (src:12589-12591)
GIVEN `the date the offence was committed or, in the case of a continuing offence, began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(8) account is taken of the offence for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF `the date the offence was committed or, in the case of a continuing offence, began` LESS THAN Date 15 5 1984
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No account is to be taken for the purposes of this section of any offence which was committed or, in the case of a continuing offence, began before 15 May 1984"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes offences before 15 May 1984 and says nothing of the others

-- (4): convicted of any 3 or more offences by virtue of any contravention of, or failure to comply with, relevant requirements counts as adjudged guilty of 3 or more.
-- src:12558 | (4) A person is to be treated as being adjudged guilty of 3 or more
-- src:12559 | offences in relation to any such relevant requirements of this Act for
-- src:12560 | the purpose of subsection (3) if the person is convicted of any 3 or
-- src:12561 | more offences by virtue of any contravention of, or failure to comply
-- src:12566 | with, any such requirements (whether on the person’s own part or on
-- src:12567 | the part of any company).
@ref s 155(4) (src:12558-12567)
GIVEN `the number of offences of which the person is convicted by virtue of contraventions of, or failures to comply with, relevant requirements, whether on the person's own part or on the part of any company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(4) the person is treated as being adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences in relation to relevant requirements` MEANS
    IF `the number of offences of which the person is convicted by virtue of contraventions of, or failures to comply with, relevant requirements, whether on the person's own part or on the part of any company` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is to be treated as being adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences ... if the person is convicted of any 3 or more offences" -- a condition introduced with "if" that fails (marginal reading (a))

-- (3): persistent default may, subject to (8), be conclusively proved by showing that within a period of 5 years the person has been adjudged guilty of
-- 3 or more offences or has had 3 or more orders under s 13 or 399 made. The counts already leave out what (5) and (8) exclude.
-- src:12550 | (3) For the purposes of this section, the fact that a person has been
-- src:12551 | persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements of this Act
-- src:12552 | may, subject to subsection (8), be conclusively proved by showing
-- src:12553 | that, within a period of 5 years, the person has been adjudged guilty of
-- src:12554 | 3 or more offences in relation to any such requirements or has had 3 or
-- src:12555 | more orders made against the person under section 13 or 399 in
-- src:12556 | relation to those requirements.
@ref s 155(3) (src:12550-12556)
GIVEN `the number of offences in relation to relevant requirements of which the person has been adjudged guilty within a period of 5 years` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of orders under section 13 or 399 in relation to relevant requirements that have been made against the person within a period of 5 years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(3) the person's persistent default in relation to relevant requirements is conclusively proved` MEANS
    IF    `the number of offences in relation to relevant requirements of which the person has been adjudged guilty within a period of 5 years` AT LEAST 3
       OR `the number of orders under section 13 or 399 in relation to relevant requirements that have been made against the person within a period of 5 years` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may ... be conclusively proved by showing" names one way of proving it and does not say that default is not persistent otherwise

-- (1): the offence of a person persistently in default who, within 5 years after last being adjudged guilty or last having an order made, without the permission of the Court,
-- is a director or promoter of, or concerned in the management of, a company.
-- src:12532 | 155.—(1) Where a person has been persistently in default in
-- src:12533 | relation to relevant requirements of this Act and that person, within a
-- src:12534 | period of 5 years after the person has last been adjudged guilty of any
-- src:12535 | offence or has had made against the person an order under section 13
-- src:12536 | or 399 in relation to any such relevant requirements of this Act,
-- src:12537 | without the permission of the Court, is a director or promoter of, or is
-- src:12538 | in any way directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the
-- src:12539 | management of a company, that person shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:12540 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:12541 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 155(1) (src:12532-12541)
GIVEN `the person has been persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person was last adjudged guilty of an offence or last had an order made under section 13 or 399 in relation to such relevant requirements` IS A DATE
      `the date the person is a director or promoter of, or is concerned in the management of, a company` IS A DATE
      `the person is in any way a director or promoter of, or directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the management of, a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person has been persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements of this Act`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the person was last adjudged guilty of an offence or last had an order made under section 13 or 399 in relation to such relevant requirements` `the date the person is a director or promoter of, or is concerned in the management of, a company` 5 Years
      AND `the person is in any way a director or promoter of, or directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the management of, a company`
      AND (NOT `the person has the permission of the Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Where a person has been persistently in default ... and that person, within a period of 5 years after ..., without the permission of the Court, is a director or promoter of ... a company, that person shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 155(1) (src:12532-12541)
GIVEN `the person has been persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person was last adjudged guilty of an offence or last had an order made under section 13 or 399 in relation to such relevant requirements` IS A DATE
      `the date the person is a director or promoter of, or is concerned in the management of, a company` IS A DATE
      `the person is in any way a director or promoter of, or directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the management of, a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155(1) penalty`
`s 155(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 155(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person has been persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements of this Act` `the date the person was last adjudged guilty of an offence or last had an order made under section 13 or 399 in relation to such relevant requirements` `the date the person is a director or promoter of, or is concerned in the management of, a company` `the person is in any way a director or promoter of, or directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the management of, a company` `the person has the permission of the Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 155(1) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (6) a person who has had a third or subsequent order under s 13 or 399 and is disqualified by this section may comply with the order.
-- src:12573 | (6) Where a person has had a third or subsequent order made
-- src:12574 | against the person under section 13 or 399 and by virtue of the
-- src:12575 | operation of this section that person is disqualified from being a
-- src:12576 | director or promoter of or from being in any way directly or indirectly
-- src:12577 | concerned or taking part in the management of a company, nothing in
-- src:12578 | this section is to be construed as preventing that person from
-- src:12579 | complying with the order of the Court and for this purpose that person
-- src:12580 | is deemed to have the same status, powers and duties as that person
-- src:12581 | had at the time the act, matter or thing should have been done.
@ref s 155(6) (src:12573-12581)
GIVEN `the person has had a third or subsequent order made against the person under section 13 or 399` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of the operation of section 155 the person is disqualified from being a director or promoter of, or from being in any way concerned or taking part in the management of, a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(6) the section prevents the person from complying with the order of the Court` MEANS
    IF `the person has had a third or subsequent order made against the person under section 13 or 399` AND `by virtue of the operation of section 155 the person is disqualified from being a director or promoter of, or from being in any way concerned or taking part in the management of, a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section is to be construed as preventing that person from complying with the order of the Court and ... that person is deemed to have the same status, powers and duties as that person had at the time the act, matter or thing should have been done"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person has had a third or subsequent order made ... and ... is disqualified" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (7) the Registrar's certificate is prima facie evidence.
-- src:12583 | (7) For the purpose of this section, a certificate of the Registrar
-- src:12584 | stating that a person has been adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences or
-- src:12585 | has had made against the person 3 or more orders under section 13 or
-- src:12586 | 399 in relation to the requirements of this Act shall in all courts be
-- src:12587 | received as prima facie evidence of the facts stated therein.
@ref s 155(7) (src:12583-12587)
GIVEN `the certificate of the Registrar states that the person has been adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences or has had made against the person 3 or more orders under section 13 or 399 in relation to the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(7) the certificate of the Registrar is received in all courts as prima facie evidence of the facts stated` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of the Registrar states that the person has been adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences or has had made against the person 3 or more orders under section 13 or 399 in relation to the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate of the Registrar stating that a person has been adjudged guilty of 3 or more offences or has had made against the person 3 or more orders" -- other certificates are not said to be evidence

-- (9) a person intending to apply for permission must give the Minister not less than 14 days' notice; (10) the Minister may be represented and may oppose.
-- src:12593 | (9) A person intending to apply for permission of the Court under
-- src:12594 | this section must give to the Minister not less than 14 days’ notice of
-- src:12595 | the person’s intention so to apply.
@ref s 155(9) (src:12593-12595)
GIVEN `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(9) the person has given the Minister the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies to the Court` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give to the Minister not less than 14 days' notice of the person's intention so to apply" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:12599 | (10) On the hearing of any application under this section, the
-- src:12600 | Minister may be represented and may oppose the granting of the
-- src:12601 | application.
@ref s 155(10) (src:12599-12601)
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under section 155` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(10) the Minister may be represented and may oppose the granting of the application` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is of an application under section 155`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of any application under this section, the Minister may be represented and may oppose" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- (11) "company" includes an unregistered company within the meaning of s 245(1) of the 2018 Act.
-- src:12603 | (11) In this section, company includes an unregistered company
-- src:12604 | within the meaning of section 245(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring
-- src:12605 | and Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 155(11) (src:12603-12605)
GIVEN `the body is an unregistered company within the meaning of section 245(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(11) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF `the body is an unregistered company within the meaning of section 245(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "company includes an unregistered company" leaves the list open

DECLARE `s 155(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 155(1) be a director or promoter of, or take part in the management of, a company without the permission of the Court, while persistently in default`

-- src:12532 | 155.—(1) Where a person has been persistently in default in
-- src:12533 | relation to relevant requirements of this Act and that person, within a
-- src:12534 | period of 5 years after the person has last been adjudged guilty of any
-- src:12535 | offence or has had made against the person an order under section 13
-- src:12536 | or 399 in relation to any such relevant requirements of this Act,
-- src:12537 | without the permission of the Court, is a director or promoter of, or is
-- src:12538 | in any way directly or indirectly concerned or takes part in the
-- src:12539 | management of a company, that person shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:12540 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:12541 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 155(1) (src:12532-12541)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 155(1) act`
`s 155(1) a person persistently in default must not be a director or take part in the management of a company without permission` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 155(1) be a director or promoter of, or take part in the management of, a company without the permission of the Court, while persistently in default`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person persistently in default in relation to relevant requirements was a director or promoter of, or took part in the management of, a company without the permission of the Court"

§ `Section 155A: a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years`

DECLARE `s 155A(2) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1A): the period of the disqualification: 5 years where the person had previously been disqualified under the section, otherwise 3 years,
-- after the date on which the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register.
-- src:12633 | (1A) The period mentioned in subsection (1) is —
-- src:12635 | (a) where the person had previously been disqualified under
-- src:12636 | this section (whether before, on or after the date of
-- src:12637 | commencement of section 5 of the Companies, Business
-- src:12638 | Trusts and Other Bodies (Miscellaneous Amendments)
-- src:12639 | Act 2023) from acting as director of, or taking part in or
-- src:12640 | being concerned in the management of, any company or
-- src:12641 | any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11
-- src:12642 | applies, 5 years after the date on which the name (or
-- src:12643 | names) of the last of the companies mentioned in
-- src:12644 | subsection (1)(a) was (or were) struck off the register; or
-- src:12646 | (b) in any other case, 3 years after the date on which the name
-- src:12647 | (or names) of the last of the companies mentioned in
-- src:12648 | subsection (1)(a) was (or were) struck off the register.
@ref s 155A(1A) (src:12633-12648)
GIVEN `the person had previously been disqualified under section 155A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 155A(1A) the last day of the period of the disqualification` MEANS
    IF `the person had previously been disqualified under section 155A`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register` 5 Years
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register` 3 Years

-- (1): a person who had been a director of 3 or more companies whose names were struck off under s 344(4) read with s 344(1) within 5 years,
-- and was a director of each at the time, must not act as director of, or be concerned in the management of, any company for the period in (1A).
-- src:12615 | 155A.—(1) A person who —
-- src:12617 | (a) had been a director of 3 or more companies which names
-- src:12618 | had been struck off the register under section 344(4) read
-- src:12619 | with section 344(1) within a period of 5 years; and
-- src:12621 | (b) was, at the time the name of each company mentioned in
-- src:12622 | paragraph (a) was struck off the register under
-- src:12623 | section 344(4) read with section 344(1), a director of the
-- src:12624 | company,
-- src:12626 | must not act as director of, or in any way (whether directly or
-- src:12627 | indirectly) take part in or be concerned in the management of, any
-- src:12628 | company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11
-- src:12629 | applies for the period specified in subsection (1A).
@ref s 155A(1) (src:12615-12629)
GIVEN `the number of companies whose names were struck off the register under section 344(4) read with section 344(1) within a period of 5 years and of each of which the person was a director when its name was struck off` IS A NUMBER
      `the person had previously been disqualified under section 155A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the body is a company or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a director or taking part in the management of the company` MEANS
    IF `the number of companies whose names were struck off the register under section 344(4) read with section 344(1) within a period of 5 years and of each of which the person was a director when its name was struck off` LESS THAN 3
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who (a) had been a director of 3 or more companies which names had been struck off ...; and (b) was ... a director of the company" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT MOST `s 155A(1A) the last day of the period of the disqualification` `the person had previously been disqualified under section 155A` `the date the name of the last of the companies was struck off the register`
          THEN (IF `the body is a company or a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies" names the bodies and says nothing of others
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period specified in subsection (1A)" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:12652 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:12653 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:12654 | $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:12655 | both.
@ref s 155A(2) (src:12652-12655)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 155A(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 155A(2) (src:12652-12655)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 155A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 155A(2) penalty`
`s 155A(2) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 155A(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes section 155A(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 155A(2) penalty` OF 10000, 2 TIMES 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (2 TIMES 12 months) or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (3), (3A): permission may be sought from the Registrar, or from the Court on 14 days' notice to the Minister; the Court route is closed while a Registrar application is pending.
DECLARE `s 155A(3) the body applied to` IS ONE OF
    `s 155A(3)(a) the Registrar`
    `s 155A(3)(b) the Court`

-- (3A): an application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an application has been made to the Registrar under (3)(a) and the Registrar's decision is pending; subsection (3) takes this as its bar.
-- src:12676 | (3A) An application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an
-- src:12677 | application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a)
-- src:12678 | and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending.
@ref s 155A(3A) (src:12676-12678)
GIVEN `an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(3A) an application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending" -- a bar with an "if" gate; outside it the subsection is silent

-- src:12662 | (3) A person who is subject to a disqualification under
-- src:12663 | subsection (1) may apply for permission to act as director of, or to
-- src:12664 | take part in or be concerned in the management of, a company or a
-- src:12665 | foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies during the
-- src:12666 | period of disqualification to —
-- src:12668 | (a) the Registrar; or
-- src:12670 | (b) the Court, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days’
-- src:12671 | notice of the person’s intention to apply for such
-- src:12672 | permission.
@ref s 155A(3) (src:12662-12672)
GIVEN `the person is subject to a disqualification under section 155A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body applied to` IS A `s 155A(3) the body applied to`
      `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date the person applies` IS A DATE
      `an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(3) the person may apply for permission to act as a director or to take part in the management of a company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is subject to a disqualification under section 155A(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to a disqualification under subsection (1) may apply" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the body applied to`
         WHEN `s 155A(3)(a) the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 155A(3)(b) the Court` THEN
              IF `s 155A(3A) an application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made` `an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (3)(b) cannot be made if an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection (3)(a) and the decision of the Registrar on the application is pending" (subsection (3A))
              ELSE (IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the person gave the Minister notice of the intention to apply` `the date the person applies` 14 Days
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court, upon giving the Minister not less than 14 days' notice" -- an "upon" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

-- src:12682 | (3B) An application under subsection (3)(a) may be granted by the
-- src:12683 | Registrar if the Registrar, having regard to such considerations as
-- src:12684 | may be prescribed, thinks fit to do so.
@ref s 155A(3B) (src:12682-12684)
GIVEN `the Registrar, having regard to such considerations as may be prescribed, thinks fit to grant the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(3B) the Registrar may grant the application under subsection (3)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar, having regard to such considerations as may be prescribed, thinks fit to grant the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be granted by the Registrar if the Registrar, having regard to such considerations as may be prescribed, thinks fit" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- src:12688 | (3C) An application under subsection (3)(b) may be granted by the
-- src:12689 | Court if the Court thinks fit to do so.
@ref s 155A(3C) (src:12688-12689)
GIVEN `the Court thinks fit to grant the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(3C) the Court may grant the application under subsection (3)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the Court thinks fit to grant the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be granted by the Court if the Court thinks fit to do so" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- src:12693 | (4) On the hearing of any application under this section, the
-- src:12694 | Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the
-- src:12695 | granting of the application.
@ref s 155A(4) (src:12693-12695)
GIVEN `the hearing is of an application under section 155A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155A(4) the Minister may be represented at the hearing and may oppose the granting of the application` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is of an application under section 155A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of any application under this section, the Minister may be represented" -- an "on" gate (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) that fails; a "may" with such a gate: split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md

DECLARE `s 155A(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 155A(1) act as a director of, or take part in the management of, a company during the period of the disqualification`

-- src:12615 | 155A.—(1) A person who —
-- src:12617 | (a) had been a director of 3 or more companies which names
-- src:12618 | had been struck off the register under section 344(4) read
-- src:12619 | with section 344(1) within a period of 5 years; and
-- src:12621 | (b) was, at the time the name of each company mentioned in
-- src:12622 | paragraph (a) was struck off the register under
-- src:12623 | section 344(4) read with section 344(1), a director of the
-- src:12624 | company,
-- src:12626 | must not act as director of, or in any way (whether directly or
-- src:12627 | indirectly) take part in or be concerned in the management of, any
-- src:12628 | company or any foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11
-- src:12629 | applies for the period specified in subsection (1A).
@ref s 155A(1) (src:12615-12629)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 155A(1) act`
`s 155A(1) a person who was a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years must not act as a director` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 155A(1) act as a director of, or take part in the management of, a company during the period of the disqualification`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person who was a director of 3 or more companies struck off within 5 years acted as a director of, or took part in the management of, a company during the period of the disqualification"
